==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-opt|pt}} {{term|tomar|lang=roa-opt}}, of {{unk.|pt|title=unknown}} origin. Possibly derived from {{etyl|la|pt}} {{term|autumo|autumāre|I reckon; I affirm|lang=la}}<ref>Yakov Malkiel, ''Etymology''</ref>.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Portugal}} {{IPA|/tuˈmaɾ/|lang=pt}}
* {{audio|Pt tomar.ogg|Audio|lang=pt}}
* {{homophones|Tomar|lang=pt}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb|tom|ar}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=pt}} to [[take]] (something);
#: {{usex|indent=1|Fui ao banco '''tomar''' meu dinheiro.|translation=I went to the bank to '''get''' my money.|lang=pt}}
# {{context|transitive|lang=pt}} to {{l/en|steal}} (something);
#: {{usex|indent=1|O ladrão '''tomou''' todo o meu dinheiro.|translation=The thief '''has stolen''' all my money.|lang=pt}}
# {{context|transitive|lang=pt}} to consider that something or someone (direct object) is other thing or other one (''{{l/pt|por}}'');
#: {{usex|indent=1|Eu '''tomei''' a Maria por corrupta.|translation=I '''thought''' Mary was corrupt.|lang=pt}}
# {{context|transitive|lang=pt}} to {{l/en|drink}};
#: {{usex|indent=1|Eu '''tomei''' suco.|translation=I '''drank''' juice.|lang=pt}}
# {{context|intransitive|lang=pt}} to {{l/en|consume}} {{l/en|alcoholic}} {{l/en|beverages}};
#: {{usex|indent=1|Ele '''toma''' muito, durante os finais de semana.|translation=He '''drinks''' a lot on weekends.|lang=pt}}

====Synonyms====
*{{sense|to take}} {{l/pt|pegar}}
*{{sense|to steal}} {{l/pt|roubar}}
*{{sense|to consider as}} {{l/pt|considerar}} (como)
*{{sense|to drink}} {{l/pt|beber}}
*{{sense|to drink alcohol}} {{l/pt|beber}}

